            <ArticleTitle>CT evaluation of intervertebral foramina lesions with normal or non-diagnostic myelograms. Report of ten cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ten patients with radicular leg pain are reported in whom good quality myelograms were either normal or non-diagnostic of a disc or tumor. Subsequent CT examination demonstrated herniated discs (eight patients) or tumors (two patients) in the intervertebral foramen, all located too far laterally to be seen with myelography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
